---
// Educational comparison: the forecast cone of uncertainty vs the actual
// impact area. Renders a stylized SVG map plus three decision points.
const blogUrl = "/blog/how-to-read-the-hurricane-cone-of-uncertainty/";
const toolUrl = "/tools/impact-window-estimator/";
const surgeUrl = "/tools/storm-surge-checker/";
---

<section class="band cone-education" aria-labelledby="cone-ed-title">
  <div class="inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">Forecast literacy</p>
    <h2 id="cone-ed-title">Cone vs Impact: Read the Map Correctly</h2>
    <p class="answer">
      The forecast cone shows where the storm <strong>center</strong> may go. Wind, storm
      surge, and rain can reach well beyond it. Use the cone for awareness, then follow your
      official watch and warning — not the cone edge.
    </p>

    <div class="cone-layout">
      <figure class="cone-figure">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 680 460" role="img" aria-labelledby="cone-svg-title cone-svg-desc">
          <title id="cone-svg-title">Hurricane forecast cone compared with the actual impact area</title>
          <desc id="cone-svg-desc">
            A cone of uncertainty extends from a hurricane at sea toward the coast. The
            impact area for wind, surge, and rain is wider than the cone and reaches a city
            outside it.
          </desc>

          <!-- ocean -->
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="680" height="460" fill="#dcecef" />

          <!-- land -->
          <path
            d="M 0 0 L 262 0 L 306 118 L 258 232 L 292 344 L 244 460 L 0 460 Z"
            fill="#e9dfc2"
            stroke="#cdbf93"
            stroke-width="2"
          />

          <!-- impact layer: wider than the cone -->
          <path
            id="impact-layer"
            class="impact-layer"
            d="M 555 95 C 400 158, 280 208, 130 258 L 104 342 C 282 382, 432 320, 555 95 Z"
            fill="#e8a33d"
            opacity="0.30"
          />

          <!-- forecast cone -->
          <path
            class="cone-layer"
            d="M 545 110 C 450 180, 340 225, 212 275 L 242 355 C 382 300, 472 240, 545 110 Z"
            fill="#3f8db0"
            opacity="0.45"
          />

          <!-- best-track center line -->
          <path
            class="track-line"
            d="M 545 110 C 445 195, 330 250, 205 335"
            fill="none"
            stroke="#20384d"
            stroke-width="3"
            stroke-dasharray="8 6"
            stroke-linecap="round"
          />

          <!-- hurricane label -->
          <g class="svg-label" transform="translate(498, 88)">
            <text x="0" y="0">Hurricane</text>
            <text x="0" y="14" class="sub">(center path)</text>
          </g>

          <!-- city A: inside cone -->
          <g class="city-marker" transform="translate(215, 310)">
            <circle r="8" fill="#c1442e" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2" />
            <text x="12" y="4">City A</text>
            <text x="12" y="18" class="sub">inside the cone</text>
          </g>

          <!-- city B: outside cone, still inside impact area -->
          <g class="city-marker" transform="translate(300, 188)">
            <circle r="8" fill="#b34a1f" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2" />
            <text x="12" y="4">City B</text>
            <text x="12" y="18" class="sub">outside cone, still at risk</text>
          </g>

          <!-- city C: far away -->
          <g class="city-marker" transform="translate(118, 128)">
            <circle r="8" fill="#0e6f8f" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2" />
            <text x="12" y="4">City C</text>
            <text x="12" y="18" class="sub">lower risk</text>
          </g>

          <!-- legend -->
          <g transform="translate(24, 428)">
            <rect x="0" y="0" width="22" height="12" fill="#3f8db0" opacity="0.6" />
            <text x="30" y="11">Forecast cone (~2/3 of centers)</text>
            <rect x="250" y="0" width="22" height="12" fill="#e8a33d" opacity="0.55" />
            <text x="280" y="11">Wind / surge / rain impact</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>
          Stylized example: City B is outside the cone yet inside the impact area.
          Watches and warnings are based on expected impacts, not the cone edge.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="cone-points">
        <article class="panel cone-point">
          <h3>1 · The cone is only about the center</h3>
          <p>
            About two-thirds of forecast track centers stay inside the cone. The other third
            land outside it. A storm's size, wind field, surge, and rain are not drawn inside
            the cone at all.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="panel cone-point">
          <h3>2 · Impacts reach beyond the cone</h3>
          <p>
            Tropical-storm-force winds, storm surge, and heavy rain routinely affect areas
            far outside the cone. Being outside the cone is not the same as being safe.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="panel cone-point">
          <h3>3 · Follow watches and warnings</h3>
          <p>
            The NHC impact map and NWS watches/warnings are based on expected impacts. Check
            your local warning, not just where the center line points.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="section-actions">
      <a class="action-link" href={blogUrl}>Read the full cone guide</a>
      <a class="action-link cone-secondary" href={toolUrl}>Estimate your impact window</a>
      <a class="action-link cone-secondary" href={surgeUrl}>Check storm surge for my ZIP</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cone-education {
    background: var(--navy);
    color: #fff;
  }

  .cone-education .eyebrow {
    color: #a6dae8;
  }

  .cone-education .answer {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
  }

  .cone-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(300px, 0.65fr);
    gap: clamp(20px, 3vw, 32px);
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: 26px;
  }

  .cone-figure {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 12px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.22);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .cone-figure svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  .cone-figure figcaption {
    margin: 10px 2px 2px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .svg-label text,
  .city-marker text {
    fill: #20384d;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .svg-label .sub,
  .city-marker .sub {
    fill: #5b6670;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .cone-points {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .cone-point {
    /* Fixed light card on the dark band — independent of theme variables. */
    background: #ffffff;
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28);
    box-shadow: var(--soft-shadow);
  }

  .cone-point h3 {
    color: #17212b;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .cone-point p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #17212b;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .cone-secondary {
    background: var(--navy);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
  }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .cone-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
